No git origin remote exists at build time by design. The GitHub origin remote is owned and added by the downstream deploy-to-github phase per pipeline skill-ownership (it creates the repo, adds origin, pushes, and renders the README/claims tables). The build phase runs local-only — it commits product + docs to the local repository but never creates or pushes to a remote — so no origin remote is present yet when ship-check runs at the build/verify boundary. This waiver records that the missing origin is the expected local-only build state, not a hygiene defect; it is resolved when deploy-to-github runs.
